36 commands and verbs

$ gate-inbox sessions -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: gate-inbox sessions [--parent <id|me>] [--status <state>] [--include-archived] [--limit <n>] [--json]
  -include-archived
    	also list rows archived out of the active list, which on an old board are most of them
  -json
    	print the raw result as JSON instead of a sentence
  -limit int
    	how many rows to print, at most 500; the last line says what was left out (default 50)
  -parent string
    	keep only the sessions one spawned; "me" is this session's own children
  -status value
    	state to keep, repeatable or comma separated: starting, working, waiting, finished, idle, errored or dead

$ gate-inbox spawn -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: gate-inbox spawn [--name <name>] [--prompt <text>] [--tool <cli>] [--model <model>] [--group <path>] [--directory <path>] [--nest] [--json]
  -account string
    	named subscription it runs on, read from Secret Manager at launch; omit for the board's default account
  -directory string
    	existing directory it works in; defaults to yours, or to the group's inherited path
  -group string
    	existing group path for a detached (--nest=false) session; a nested one is always in yours
  -json
    	print the raw result as JSON instead of a sentence
  -model string
    	model that CLI should run on, in its own names; omit for the CLI's default
  -name string
    	kebab-case name naming the work it will do; the new agent names itself when this is empty
  -nest
    	file it under this session, where its questions and rests reach you; --nest=false detaches it, for work that is not yours (default true)
  -prompt string
    	first task to hand it, written as a full instruction, since it cannot see your conversation
  -tool string
    	agent CLI to run; defaults to the CLI this session runs

$ gate-inbox send -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: gate-inbox send <session-id> "<message>" [--subject <label>] [--interrupt] [--as-human] [--json]
  -as-human
    	deliver as your own words rather than fenced as a message from another agent; for a person at a terminal, and refused from an agent's shell
  -interrupt
    	stop the session's running turn first so this is its next turn; refused for a CLI with no interrupt_keys, and never sent over a dialog
  -json
    	print the raw result as JSON instead of a sentence
  -subject string
    	label for what this message is about; your next message to the same session under the same label replaces this one while it is still unread

